Package: fancyfx
Title: Publication-Ready Effect Plots for Statistical Models
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Camille", "Ross", email = "camille.ross@maine.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1428-2294"))
Description: Turns fitted models into figures ready for a manuscript. Plots the
    effect of a predictor with a rug of the raw data stacked directly above it,
    so a bend in the curve can be read against how much data supports it.
    Defaults are chosen for publication rather than for exploration: a clean
    theme with no grid or background panel, lettered panel labels, and a
    categorical palette checked for legibility under colour vision deficiency.
    Works across model types: generalized additive models fitted with 'mgcv' are
    shown as partial effects via 'gratia', and other models -- including mixed
    and Bayesian fits -- as predictions via 'marginaleffects'. Provides control
    over individual terms, factor-smooth interactions, several rug styles,
    variable transformations, and multi-panel layouts comparing either several
    predictors or several competing models.
